2025-05-01 03:12:35 - Thread-1219 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage for solving the task  
• match.match_id : “glue” key that lets us tie every other table back to a particular game  
• match.season_id : filter only the rows that belong to season 5 (WHERE "season_id" = 5)  
• ball_by_ball.match_id / over_id / ball_id : three–part key to marry ball‑by‑ball information with the batsman_scored table  
• ball_by_ball.striker : the player_id of the batsman who faced the ball (used to attribute the runs)  
• batsman_scored.runs_scored : the number of runs made off that ball (add them up for each striker)  
• player_match.match_id & player_match.player_id : quickest way to count how many different matches each player appeared in (needed for “per‑match” average)  
• player.player_id : join field that links a player to every other table  
• player.player_name : the human‑readable name we must finally display  

Typical conditions that will be needed  
• "season_id" = 5 (keep only season 5)  
• JOIN clauses on ("match_id", "over_id", "ball_id") between ball_by_ball and batsman_scored  
• GROUP BY striker / player_id when totalling runs  
• COUNT(DISTINCT "match_id") to compute the number of matches a player took part in  

Below are 10 exploratory SQLite queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progress from the simplest inspection to the full answer.  
Every query is preceded by a short description comment.

```sql
--Description: 1) List all seasons that exist in the match table
SELECT DISTINCT "season_id"
FROM "match"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Show a few matches that belong to season 5
SELECT DISTINCT "match_id", "match_date"
FROM "match"
WHERE "season_id" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Count how many matches were played in season 5
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "match_id") AS "match_count"
FROM "match"
WHERE "season_id" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Inspect ball‑by‑ball records tied to season 5 matches
SELECT DISTINCT b."match_id", b."over_id", b."ball_id", b."striker"
FROM "ball_by_ball" AS b
JOIN "match"       AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
WHERE m."season_id" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) View runs scored on each ball together with the striker (season 5 only)
SELECT DISTINCT b."match_id", b."over_id", b."ball_id",
       b."striker", r."runs_scored"
FROM "ball_by_ball"   AS b
JOIN "batsman_scored" AS r
  ON r."match_id" = b."match_id"
 AND r."over_id"  = b."over_id"
 AND r."ball_id"  = b."ball_id"
JOIN "match" AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
WHERE m."season_id" = 5
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Total runs made by each player (striker) in season 5
SELECT b."striker" AS "player_id",
       SUM(r."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
FROM "ball_by_ball"   AS b
JOIN "batsman_scored" AS r
  ON r."match_id" = b."match_id"
 AND r."over_id"  = b."over_id"
 AND r."ball_id"  = b."ball_id"
JOIN "match" AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
WHERE m."season_id" = 5
GROUP BY b."striker"
ORDER BY "total_runs" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Count how many season‑5 matches each player appeared in
SELECT pm."player_id",
       COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played"
FROM "player_match" AS pm
JOIN "match"        AS m ON m."match_id" = pm."match_id"
WHERE m."season_id" = 5
GROUP BY pm."player_id"
ORDER BY "matches_played" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Compute batting average (runs ÷ matches) for every player in season 5
SELECT t."player_id",
       1.0 * t."total_runs" / mp."matches_played" AS "avg_runs_per_match"
FROM (
        SELECT b."striker" AS "player_id",
               SUM(r."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
        FROM "ball_by_ball"   AS b
        JOIN "batsman_scored" AS r
          ON r."match_id" = b."match_id"
         AND r."over_id"  = b."over_id"
         AND r."ball_id"  = b."ball_id"
        JOIN "match" AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
        WHERE m."season_id" = 5
        GROUP BY b."striker"
     ) AS t
JOIN (
        SELECT pm."player_id",
               COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played"
        FROM "player_match" AS pm
        JOIN "match"        AS m ON m."match_id" = pm."match_id"
        WHERE m."season_id" = 5
        GROUP BY pm."player_id"
     ) AS mp
ON mp."player_id" = t."player_id"
ORDER BY "avg_runs_per_match" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Bring in player names and list the overall top 5 averages for season 5
SELECT p."player_name",
       a."avg_runs_per_match"
FROM (
        SELECT t."player_id",
               1.0 * t."total_runs" / mp."matches_played" AS "avg_runs_per_match"
        FROM (
                SELECT b."striker" AS "player_id",
                       SUM(r."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
                FROM "ball_by_ball"   AS b
                JOIN "batsman_scored" AS r
                  ON r."match_id" = b."match_id"
                 AND r."over_id"  = b."over_id"
                 AND r."ball_id"  = b."ball_id"
                JOIN "match" AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
                WHERE m."season_id" = 5
                GROUP BY b."striker"
             ) AS t
        JOIN (
                SELECT pm."player_id",
                       COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played"
                FROM "player_match" AS pm
                JOIN "match"        AS m ON m."match_id" = pm."match_id"
                WHERE m."season_id" = 5
                GROUP BY pm."player_id"
             ) AS mp
        ON mp."player_id" = t."player_id"
     ) AS a
JOIN "player" AS p ON p."player_id" = a."player_id"
ORDER BY a."avg_runs_per_match" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Same as #9 but also show total runs & matches for extra context
SELECT p."player_name",
       stats."total_runs",
       stats."matches_played",
       stats."avg_runs_per_match"
FROM (
       SELECT t."player_id",
              t."total_runs",
              mp."matches_played",
              1.0 * t."total_runs" / mp."matches_played" AS "avg_runs_per_match"
       FROM (
               SELECT b."striker" AS "player_id",
                      SUM(r."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
               FROM "ball_by_ball"   AS b
               JOIN "batsman_scored" AS r
                 ON r."match_id" = b."match_id"
                AND r."over_id"  = b."over_id"
                AND r."ball_id"  = b."ball_id"
               JOIN "match" AS m ON m."match_id" = b."match_id"
               WHERE m."season_id" = 5
               GROUP BY b."striker"
            ) AS t
       JOIN (
               SELECT pm."player_id",
                      COUNT(DISTINCT pm."match_id") AS "matches_played"
               FROM "player_match" AS pm
               JOIN "match"        AS m ON m."match_id" = pm."match_id"
               WHERE m."season_id" = 5
               GROUP BY pm."player_id"
            ) AS mp
       ON mp."player_id" = t."player_id"
     ) AS stats
JOIN "player" AS p ON p."player_id" = stats."player_id"
ORDER BY stats."avg_runs_per_match" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

Running the last query (#9 or #10) will directly give the requested final list: the names of the five best batters in season 5 together with their average runs per match.
